      <h1>Parallel pathways</h1>
      <p class="lead">A single workplace event can raise several legal questions. This map is a screening tool, not a conclusion that every pathway applies.</p>
      <div class="notice">Training material only — not legal advice. The applicable source may be legislation, an award, enterprise agreement, contract, policy, evidence or case-specific advice.</div>
      <div class="pathway-grid">
        <a href="/modules/who-can-claim"><b>Unfair dismissal</b><small>Eligibility, dismissal, s.387 merits and remedy.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/general-protections"><b>General protections</b><small>Workplace rights, protected activity, adverse action and reverse onus.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/medical-capacity"><b>Capacity and disability</b><small>Inherent requirements, medical evidence, adjustment and discrimination risk.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/safety-breaches"><b>WHS and psychosocial risk</b><small>Immediate controls, consultation, incident evidence and the separate disciplinary question.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/agreements-and-policies"><b>Industrial instruments and contract</b><small>Procedures, standards, consultation and contractual limits.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/drug-and-alcohol"><b>Fitness for work</b><small>Testing authority, impairment, policy, privacy and medical context.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/bullying-and-harassment"><b>Bullying and harassment</b><small>Complaint, positive-duty, discrimination, WHS and disciplinary pathways.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/absenteeism-and-abandonment"><b>Leave and attendance</b><small>Protected absence, workers compensation, incapacity, absenteeism and abandonment.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/social-media-and-out-of-hours"><b>Protected expression</b><small>Workplace rights, industrial activity, political opinion, privacy and connection to work.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/notice-and-summary-dismissal"><b>Notice and summary dismissal</b><small>Notice, serious misconduct and the source of any summary-dismissal power.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/commission-proceedings"><b>Commission process</b><small>Jurisdiction, representation, conciliation, remedy and costs.</small></a>
        <a href="/modules/records-that-stand-up"><b>Evidence and records</b><small>Preservation, authenticity, access, chronology and what the decision-maker actually knew.</small></a>
      </div>
      <h2>Use the map without turning it into a checklist</h2>
      <p>The point is not to complete every box. It is to avoid treating an issue as a simple conduct or performance matter when the facts may engage another source or protection.</p>
      <ul class="principles compact"><li>Identify the obvious pathway.</li><li>Ask what fact would activate a second pathway.</li><li>Check the source that governs that pathway.</li><li>Keep unresolved pathways visible while the facts are tested.</li></ul>
